<!-- Next Transfer notification small icon — owner decision (2026-09-22).

     WHY THIS REPLACED THE PREVIOUS ARTWORK.  The post-P2 audit proved the
     reported green notification glyph was a COLOUR problem (no notification
     colour and no theme colorAccent, so Android tinted the monochrome icon with
     `@color/material_deep_teal_500` #ff008577 — fixed separately by passing an
     explicit brand tint), but it also confirmed the old artwork could never read
     cleanly at notification size: it was the full traced "hand + notebook"
     illustration at 24dp, drawn as many thin outlined strokes that collapse into
     a blob once the system scales them down and tints them.

     Android has one hard law for a small icon: it must be a monochrome,
     white-on-transparent silhouette whose ALPHA is the shape.  The system
     discards RGB, recolours the alpha with the notification tint, and never
     draws a background.  So the mark must be a few SOLID shapes, not line art.

     This is the approved notebook mark REDUCED to its dominant element: one
     rounded page with a binding margin (wider left margin than right, so it
     reads as a notebook rather than a generic document) and three transparent
     writing lines cut out of it.  Three shapes, no outlines, no thin ribbons.

     RESOURCE CONTRACT — all deliberately unchanged:
       * the resource NAME stays `ic_nt_notification`, because the Dart plugin
         resolves it by name at runtime;
       * `res/raw/keep.xml` still lists `@drawable/ic_nt_notification`, which is
         what stops the release resource shrinker from stripping a drawable that
         nothing in the Android build references by name;
       * 24dp x 24dp and a transparent background stay as they were.

     SAFE INSET.  The page occupies x 5..19 and y 3..21 of the 24dp canvas: a
     3-unit margin top/bottom and 5-unit margin left/right, with a 2-unit corner
     radius.  The previous artwork used a 1.08 group scale that spent roughly
     1dp of edge clearance; this version needs none, so no platform mask or OEM
     circular backdrop can visually clip the mark.

     The writing lines are transparent cut-outs via `fillType="evenOdd"`, which
     is what keeps this ONE path and therefore ONE tinted silhouette. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
      android:fillType="evenOdd"
      android:pathData="M7,3 H17 A2,2 0 0 1 19,5 V19 A2,2 0 0 1 17,21 H7 A2,2 0 0 1 5,19 V5 A2,2 0 0 1 7,3 Z M9,7.5 H15.5 V9.5 H9 Z M9,11 H15.5 V13 H9 Z M9,14.5 H13.5 V16.5 H9 Z" />
</vector>
